<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7365" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cenchris</span></b> , ĭdis, =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεγχρίς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Fem.</i>, <i>a kind of hawk</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin. 10, 52, 73, § 143 sq.</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">29, 6, 38, §
				127</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Masc.</i> (cf. Passow under <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεγχρίας</span>), <i>a kind of spotted
			serpent</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 22, 90, § 245</span></i>
				(acc. cenchrim); <i><span class="en">Luc. 9,
			712</span></i>.</div>
